-~> Syntax errors: the parser reports each mistake with its line and
-~> column, and the program doesn't run at all, not even its first line.
-~> After an error the parser skips to the next ";" or "}" and carries on,
-~> so ending each statement with ";" lets it find all three mistakes.
-~> Run it with: go run . examples/errors/syntax.liz

